{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I will lay.</b> By way of parable, concerning the line and plumb-line of builders, because he said, \"Behold, I lay in Zion a stone.\" And some say that the stone is by way of parable concerning Hezekiah." "<b>And hail shall sweep away.</b> From the root of היעים (the sweeping waters). And hail is the agent, for \"sweep\" is an active verb, and the meaning of hail is a parable for the king of Assyria." "<b>Refuge.</b> It draws the vav after it, as in וְסֻתַּר מַחְסֵה מַיִם יִשְׁטֹפוּ, or the word אלה is elided."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:39.879884494Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}